pkg/std/os Seek/ReadAt/WriteAt pass int64 offsets, but on ILP32 arm32-linux off_t is 32-bit: a 64-bit arg shifts the lseek/pread/pwrite register-pair arg layout, corrupting the call. Flags are now correct via build.OS; the remaining blocker is off_t width (use *64 calls or a target-width off_t). See claude-todo.md.
